From 7f71af71fedce5823cafa6d79efce7c2bb56bbe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:04:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: reserve scrollbar-gutter: stable like Chrome on Linux

A scroll container with scrollbar-gutter: stable (GitLab's panels) now
reserves 15px, the width of Chrome's classic Linux scrollbars, on its
inline-end edge, and on both edges for both-edges. The gutter is laid
out as part of the border widths, so it sits between the border and the
padding, outside the scrollport and the containing block of absolutely
positioned descendants, and clientWidth/clientLeft match Chrome. With
box-sizing: content-box the gutter comes out of the specified size.
Border painting subtracts it again, and Taffy sees it in the border of
grid containers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/layout/display_list/mod.rs         |  3 +-
 components/layout/style_ext.rs                | 85 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../layout/taffy/stylo_taffy/wrapper.rs       | 40 +++++++--
 3 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

